course: dictionary
lesson: 792
title: The beech tree
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A beech is a large tree, and you can often recognise it by its smooth grey bark. Scientists also use clues like buds and shape to tell trees apart, especially in winter when the leaves have fallen. «In winter, bark, buds and shape still tell trees apart: ash has black buds, beech has long pointed buds.» So a tree with long pointed buds is probably a beech.
explain: The word beech can mean the tree or its wood. «The Mole crawls into the hollow of an old beech tree.» Here beech is the tree, because a mole can crawl into it. Wood is different: «Beech is also the hard, pale wood of this tree.» Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check by swapping in a different word.
explain: Beechnuts are small, three-sided nuts that fall from the tree. «Piles of wheat, oats, barley, beech-mast and nuts lie ready to be moved» uses beech-mast to mean these little nuts. Squirrels, mice and birds eat them, so beech trees feed many animals.
fact: A beech is a large tree with smooth grey bark and shiny oval leaves.
fact: Beech trees grow in Europe and North America.
fact: Beech is the hard, pale wood of the tree, used for furniture, spoons, chopping boards and toys.
fact: Beechnuts, also called beech mast, are small three-sided nuts eaten by squirrels, mice and birds.
fact: «Beech» can mean the tree or its wood, so use the sentence to decide which one is meant.
exercise: «The Mole crawls into the hollow of an old beech tree, trembling.» What kind of thing is a beech? | A type of cloud | A kind of stone | A small animal that lives in holes | *A large tree with smooth grey bark and shiny oval leaves
exercise: «In winter, bark, buds and shape still tell trees apart.» Which tree has long pointed buds? | Birch, which has white bark | *Beech | Oak, which has rough, cracked bark | Ash, which has black buds
exercise: «Piles of wheat, oats, barley, beech-mast and nuts lie ready to be moved.» What is beech-mast? | *The little nuts of the beech tree | A hard, pale stone | A kind of grass | Wood used for making spoons
test: Beech wood is hard and pale. Which items is it used to make? | *Spoons, chopping boards and toys | Bricks and roof tiles | Cars and bridges | Glass windows and bottles
test: Which word names the small three-sided nut of the beech? | *Beechnut | Beech bark | Beech leaf | Beechwood
exam: «The Ukrainian Carpathians have some of Europe's biggest old beech forests.» Where do beech trees grow, according to the lessons? | *Europe and North America | Only in Australia | Only in Africa | In the desert
